1
00:04:22,090 --> 00:04:23,080
Your Grace.

2
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:26,520
The trial will be getting under way soon.

3
00:04:59,650 --> 00:05:00,830
You got my money?

4
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:02,730
Later. Go away.

5
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,210
Grand Maester.

6
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,210
Ser Loras Tyrell.

7
00:06:00,710 --> 00:06:02,790
Are you prepared to stand trial

8
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:07,260
and profess your guilt or innocence before the Seven?

9
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,490
There'll be no need for a trial.

10
00:06:15,130 --> 00:06:16,730
I confess before the Seven

11
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:19,110
and freely admit to my crimes.

12
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:23,640
To which crimes will you be confessing?

13
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,510
All of them.

14
00:06:27,710 --> 00:06:28,940
I lay with other men

15
00:06:29,770 --> 00:06:32,930
including the traitor Renly Baratheon.

16
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:38,310
I perjured myself before the gods.

17
00:06:39,370 --> 00:06:41,440
I am guilty of depravity...

18
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:43,800
dishonesty,

19
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:46,590
profligacy,

20
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:48,190
and arrogance.

21
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,730
I see that now.

22
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:55,310
I humble myself before the Seven

23
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,540
and accept whatever punishment the gods deem just.

24
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:04,840
The gods' judgment is fierce,

25
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,840
but also fair.

26
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,260
The Warrior punishes those who believe themselves

27
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:14,140
beyond the reach of justice.

28
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:22,520
But the Mother shows her mercy to those who kneel before her.

29
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:34,000
I take full responsibility for my many sins

30
00:07:34,070 --> 00:07:36,310
and unburden myself of my desires.

31
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:41,500
My only remaining wish

32
00:07:43,050 --> 00:07:45,420
is to devote my life to the Seven.

33
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,770
May I be a living example of their grace

34
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:50,830
for others to witness.

35
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:56,430
You understand fully

36
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:58,040
what this means?

37
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,990
I do.

38
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,570
I will abandon the Tyrell name

39
00:08:04,930 --> 00:08:06,180
and all that goes with it.

40
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:12,040
I will renounce my lordship and my claims on Highgarden.

41
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,320
I will never marry

42
00:08:18,210 --> 00:08:19,820
and I will never father children.

43
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:25,960
Brother Loras...

44
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:30,550
...I ask you to dedicate your life to the seven gods.

45
00:08:34,850 --> 00:08:39,980
Will you fight to defend your faith against heretics and apostates?

46
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,540
I will.

47
00:09:11,310 --> 00:09:12,410
No, I can't let them--

48
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:15,190
Faith is the way, Father.

49
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,190
All right.

50
00:09:40,350 --> 00:09:41,300
I'm ready.

51
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:50,940
I have to go. I'm--

52
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:53,430
I'm late for the trial.

53
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:08,960
You mutilated him.

54
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:11,370
You gave me your word.

55
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:13,220
And I have kept my word.

56
00:10:14,070 --> 00:10:16,470
Once the queen mother's trial is concluded,

57
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,230
Brother Loras is free to leave.

58
00:10:18,230 --> 00:10:20,170
And where is the queen mother?

59
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,530
Her litter never left the Red Keep.

60
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:27,860
It appears the queen mother doesn't wish to attend her own trial.

61
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:33,000
Go to the Red Keep and show her the way.

62
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:01,040
Get the others.

63
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,970
Where's the king?

64
00:11:48,930 --> 00:11:50,480
Elsewhere, I'm afraid.

65
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:52,370
What's the meaning of this?

66
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:53,460
I was told that--

67
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,990
I have more important things to do with my time

68
00:11:57,990 --> 00:11:59,160
than waste them in the presence--

69
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:02,200
Please, Grand Maester. I bear you no ill will.

70
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,780
Please forgive me if you can.

71
00:12:38,170 --> 00:12:39,880
This pains me, my lord.

72
00:12:40,270 --> 00:12:42,130
Whatever your faults, you do not deserve

73
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:45,200
to die alone in such a cold, dark place.

74
00:12:45,590 --> 00:12:48,320
But sometimes before we can usher in the new,

75
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:52,920
the old must be put to rest.

76
00:13:34,470 --> 00:13:36,970
The longer you wait, the worse it'll be for you.

77
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:05,960
What are you doing?

78
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:15,530
There's something wrong.

79
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,650
You have nothing to fear, Your Grace.

80
00:15:18,690 --> 00:15:20,480
The trial will begin shortly.

81
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:23,400
Cersei is not here. Tommen is not here.

82
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,900
Why do you think they're not here?

83
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,690
If the accused is not here,

84
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:28,840
she will be tried regardless.

85
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:31,210
We cannot escape the justice of the gods--

86
00:15:31,210 --> 00:15:34,070
Forget about the bloody gods and listen to what I'm telling you.

87
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:37,530
Cersei understands the consequences of her absence

88
00:15:37,530 --> 00:15:39,490
and she is absent anyway,

89
00:15:39,490 --> 00:15:42,600
which means she does not intend to suffer those consequences.

90
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:47,120
The trial can wait. We all need to leave.

91
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:14,950
We all need to leave now.

92
00:16:20,110 --> 00:16:21,020
Loras.

93
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,930
Stay with me.

94
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,920
Let me through. Let me through.

95
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,770
Get out of my way.

96
00:16:52,410 --> 00:16:53,530
Let us through.

97
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,370
Confess.

98
00:18:28,330 --> 00:18:29,380
Confess.

99
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:35,980
- No. - Confess.

100
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:48,790
Confess. It felt good.

101
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:52,190
Beating me, starving me,

102
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:55,690
frightening me, humiliating me.

103
00:18:58,770 --> 00:19:01,820
You didn't do it because you cared about my atonement.

104
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:04,040
You did it because it felt good.

105
00:19:05,610 --> 00:19:06,950
I understand.

106
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,230
I do things because they feel good.

107
00:19:13,850 --> 00:19:16,100
I drink because it feels good.

108
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:20,620
I killed my husband because it felt good to be rid of him.

109
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:28,640
I fuck my brother because it feels good to feel him inside me.

110
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,300
I lie about fucking my brother...

111
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:34,900
because it feels good to keep our son

112
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,360
safe from hateful hypocrites.

113
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,120
I killed your High Sparrow...

114
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:46,150
and all his little sparrows...

115
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:50,350
all his septons, all his septas,

116
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:53,300
all his filthy soldiers,

117
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:57,140
because it felt good to watch them burn.

118
00:19:59,070 --> 00:20:02,530
It felt good to imagine their shock and their pain.

119
00:20:03,350 --> 00:20:06,160
No thought has ever given me greater joy.

120
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:15,850
Even confessing feels good under the right circumstances.

121
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,200
You've always been quiet.

122
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:34,520
I said my face would be the last thing you saw before you died.

123
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:35,670
Do you remember?

124
00:20:37,810 --> 00:20:38,760
Good.

125
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,220
I'm glad to see your face.

126
00:20:46,590 --> 00:20:48,520
I'm ready to meet the gods.

127
00:20:48,590 --> 00:20:49,660
What?

128
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:52,760
Now?

129
00:20:54,390 --> 00:20:55,350
Today?

130
00:20:58,470 --> 00:21:00,570
You're not going to die today.

131
00:21:03,690 --> 00:21:05,690
You're not going to die for quite a while.

132
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:09,420
Ser Gregor.

133
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,990
This is Ser Gregor Clegane.

134
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:18,510
He's quiet, too.

135
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,820
Your gods have forsaken you.

136
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:34,760
This is your god now.

137
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,420
No.

138
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:50,720
No.

139
00:21:52,190 --> 00:21:53,250
Shame.

140
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,530
Shame.

141
00:21:58,840 --> 00:21:59,680
Shame.

142
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:09,710
I'm very sorry, Your Grace.

143
00:22:11,570 --> 00:22:12,720
Very sorry.

144
00:22:56,910 --> 00:22:59,550
For House Lannister!

145
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:01,280
Hear me roar!

146
00:23:06,930 --> 00:23:09,320
For House Frey!

147
00:23:09,710 --> 00:23:11,550
We stand together!

148
00:23:12,530 --> 00:23:15,560
May we stand together through the centuries,

149
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:18,060
good friends to the last.

150
00:23:18,550 --> 00:23:22,220
And when we drive our swords through our enemies' hearts,

151
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:25,330
may we speak the words of our alliance,

152
00:23:26,010 --> 00:23:29,180
"The Freys and the Lannisters

153
00:23:29,890 --> 00:23:31,760
send their regards."

154
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:51,290
You don't even have to do anything, do you?

155
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:55,260
You just sit there, a rich slab of beef,

156
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:56,880
and all the birds come pecking.

157
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:59,390
- You're welcome to her. - She doesn't want me.

158
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:01,940
She wants your golden fingers up her twat.

159
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:05,520
Those two have their eyes on you.

160
00:24:08,070 --> 00:24:09,960
They have their eyes on you, cunt.

161
00:24:10,590 --> 00:24:11,880
Not my type.

162
00:24:12,060 --> 00:24:13,340
Not blonde enough?

163
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:19,140
Ladies, have you met Ser Bronn of the Blackwater,

164
00:24:19,140 --> 00:24:21,490
hero of the Battle of Blackwater Bay?

165
00:24:21,860 --> 00:24:23,790
- There you go. - Maybe I'm not in the mood.

166
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:29,040
Fuck it.

167
00:24:29,300 --> 00:24:32,120
No need to call me ser just because I'm an anointed knight.

168
00:24:37,570 --> 00:24:39,790
This came together rather well.

169
00:24:41,610 --> 00:24:43,570
Your father would be pleased.

170
00:24:43,610 --> 00:24:44,890
I'm sure he would be.

171
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,070
Edmure is back in a cell.

172
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:54,040
Can't go killing my son by law. It wouldn't be right.

173
00:24:54,810 --> 00:24:56,820
Give the family a bad name.

174
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:04,370
So the famous Blackfish killed by foot soldiers, eh?

175
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:07,300
Legendary warrior, everyone said.

176
00:25:08,990 --> 00:25:10,840
Have you done much fighting yourself, Lord Frey?

177
00:25:10,850 --> 00:25:13,540
I'm a bit old for all that.

178
00:25:13,540 --> 00:25:16,040
No, but back in your day.

179
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:19,260
The purpose of fighting

180
00:25:19,490 --> 00:25:21,900
is defeating your enemies, isn't it?

181
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:24,400
I've defeated mine.

182
00:25:25,020 --> 00:25:28,770
Riverrun belonged to House Tully for a thousand years.

183
00:25:28,770 --> 00:25:30,040
Now it's mine.

184
00:25:30,350 --> 00:25:31,980
What do you call that?

185
00:25:33,170 --> 00:25:34,000
Victory.

186
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:37,060
Yes, you're a great conqueror.

187
00:25:38,420 --> 00:25:41,510
Go on, mock me, boy. You think I mind?

188
00:25:42,210 --> 00:25:44,600
The Tullys mocked me for years.

189
00:25:45,180 --> 00:25:47,090
The Starks mocked me.

190
00:25:47,090 --> 00:25:48,470
Where are they now?

191
00:25:49,050 --> 00:25:51,450
You talk about war as if you're an expert,

192
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:53,830
but the one battle I remember you fighting,

193
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:56,890
you were captured by Robb Stark, the Young Wolf.

194
00:25:57,610 --> 00:25:58,980
But it doesn't matter.

195
00:25:59,570 --> 00:26:03,360
Here we are now, two kingslayers.

196
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:07,220
We know what it's like to have them grovel to our faces

197
00:26:07,220 --> 00:26:09,590
and snigger behind our backs.

198
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:11,900
We don't mind, do we?

199
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:15,750
Fear is a marvelous thing.

200
00:26:16,270 --> 00:26:17,780
They don't fear the Freys, though.

201
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:19,490
They fear the Lannisters.

202
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:23,180
We gave you the Riverlands to hold the Riverlands.

203
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:25,430
If we have to ride north and take them back for you

204
00:26:25,430 --> 00:26:27,130
every time you lose them,

205
00:26:28,580 --> 00:26:29,900
why do we need you?

206
00:26:52,250 --> 00:26:53,400
Show me.

207
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:58,140
Your Grace, there's no need--

208
00:26:58,140 --> 00:26:59,340
Show me.

209
00:27:12,850 --> 00:27:15,430
What are your thoughts concerning the king's funeral?

210
00:27:16,240 --> 00:27:18,970
As the Sept of Baelor is no longer an option,

211
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:22,280
perhaps a ceremony in the throne room?

212
00:27:24,140 --> 00:27:26,110
He should be with his grandfather,

213
00:27:27,870 --> 00:27:30,260
his brother, his sister.

214
00:27:32,990 --> 00:27:34,160
Burn him

215
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:38,430
and bury his ashes where the sept once stood.

216
00:28:36,150 --> 00:28:37,340
Hello.

217
00:28:44,290 --> 00:28:47,480
From Lord Commander Snow at Castle Black.

218
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:04,120
I'm--

219
00:29:04,920 --> 00:29:06,850
I'm to be the new maester.

220
00:29:24,310 --> 00:29:25,570
According to our records,

221
00:29:25,570 --> 00:29:27,730
Jeor Mormont is Lord Commander.

222
00:29:29,300 --> 00:29:30,650
He died.

223
00:29:30,650 --> 00:29:33,210
We received no report from the maester at Castle Black.

224
00:29:33,210 --> 00:29:36,910
Maester Aemon became quite ill shortly after the election.

225
00:29:37,170 --> 00:29:38,930
He's since passed away.

226
00:29:41,100 --> 00:29:43,110
Which is why I'm here.

227
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:47,940
This is irregular.

228
00:29:48,580 --> 00:29:52,740
Yes, well, I suppose that life is irregular.

229
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:07,860
The archmaester will discuss these irregularities with you.

230
00:30:11,270 --> 00:30:14,310
In the meantime, you are permitted to use the library.

231
00:30:14,820 --> 00:30:15,980
Follow me.

232
00:30:19,270 --> 00:30:20,630
No women or children.

233
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:17,170
When we had feasts,

234
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:20,040
our family would sit up here...

235
00:32:21,970 --> 00:32:23,710
and I'd sit down there.

236
00:32:26,230 --> 00:32:27,980
Could have been worse, Jon Snow.

237
00:32:29,210 --> 00:32:30,560
You had a family.

238
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:32,350
You had feasts.

239
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:36,920
Aye, you're right. I was luckier than most.

240
00:32:52,970 --> 00:32:54,230
What is that?

241
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:57,330
Tell him.

242
00:33:01,180 --> 00:33:03,200
Tell him who it belonged to.

243
00:33:08,390 --> 00:33:09,830
The Princess Shireen.

244
00:33:09,830 --> 00:33:11,410
Tell him what you did to her.

245
00:33:14,450 --> 00:33:15,720
Tell him!

246
00:33:22,450 --> 00:33:24,090
We burned her at the stake.

247
00:33:36,520 --> 00:33:37,820
Why?

248
00:33:39,610 --> 00:33:42,330
The army was trapped. The horses were dying.

249
00:33:42,550 --> 00:33:45,540
- It was the only way. - You burned a little girl alive!

250
00:33:45,540 --> 00:33:46,790
I only do what my Lord commands.

251
00:33:46,790 --> 00:33:50,580
If he commands you to burn children, your Lord is evil.

252
00:33:53,500 --> 00:33:55,670
We are standing here because of him.

253
00:33:56,720 --> 00:34:00,060
Jon Snow is alive because the Lord willed it.

254
00:34:00,060 --> 00:34:03,950
I loved that girl like she was my own.

255
00:34:04,030 --> 00:34:07,080
She was good. She was kind. And you killed her!

256
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:10,840
So did her father.

257
00:34:13,210 --> 00:34:14,620
So did her mother.

258
00:34:16,770 --> 00:34:18,980
Her own blood knew it was the only way.

259
00:34:18,980 --> 00:34:20,570
The only way for what?

260
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:23,650
They all died anyway.

261
00:34:25,390 --> 00:34:27,290
You told everyone Stannis was the one.

262
00:34:27,290 --> 00:34:29,630
You had him believing it, all of them fooled.

263
00:34:29,630 --> 00:34:31,600
- And you lied. - I didn't lie.

264
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,250
I was wrong.

265
00:34:35,250 --> 00:34:38,120
Aye, you were wrong.

266
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:42,270
How many died because you were wrong?

267
00:34:47,630 --> 00:34:51,290
I ask your leave to execute this woman for murder.

268
00:34:51,290 --> 00:34:52,890
She admits to the crime.

269
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:57,990
Do you have anything to say for yourself?

270
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:02,760
I've been ready to die for many years.

271
00:35:04,370 --> 00:35:05,690
If the Lord was done with me,

272
00:35:05,690 --> 00:35:07,390
so be it, but he's not.

273
00:35:07,810 --> 00:35:10,280
You've seen the Night King, Jon Snow.

274
00:35:11,170 --> 00:35:13,660
You know the great war is still to come.

275
00:35:14,390 --> 00:35:17,280
You know the army of the dead will be upon us soon.

276
00:35:18,390 --> 00:35:21,240
And you know I can help you win that war.

277
00:35:35,560 --> 00:35:37,210
Ride south today.

278
00:35:38,560 --> 00:35:40,400
If you return to the North,

279
00:35:40,770 --> 00:35:42,930
I'll have you hanged as a murderer.

280
00:36:00,900 --> 00:36:03,650
If you ever come back this way,

281
00:36:03,660 --> 00:36:05,980
I will execute you myself.

282
00:36:38,430 --> 00:36:40,670
I'm having the lord's chamber prepared for you.

283
00:36:42,650 --> 00:36:44,290
Mother and Father's room?

284
00:36:46,200 --> 00:36:47,640
You should take it.

285
00:36:49,410 --> 00:36:50,850
I'm not a Stark.

286
00:36:52,180 --> 00:36:53,490
You are to me.

287
00:36:57,990 --> 00:36:59,420
You're the Lady of Winterfell.

288
00:36:59,420 --> 00:37:01,780
You deserve it. We're standing here because of you.

289
00:37:03,290 --> 00:37:05,970
The battle was lost until the Knights of the Vale rode in.

290
00:37:06,730 --> 00:37:08,270
They came because of you.

291
00:37:12,890 --> 00:37:15,380
You told me Lord Baelish sold you to the Boltons.

292
00:37:16,340 --> 00:37:17,950
- He did. - And you trust him?

293
00:37:19,380 --> 00:37:21,670
Only a fool would trust Littlefinger.

294
00:37:25,010 --> 00:37:26,850
I should have told you about him,

295
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,810
about the Knights of the Vale.

296
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,780
I'm sorry.

297
00:37:44,070 --> 00:37:45,910
We need to trust each other.

298
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:48,860
We can't fight a war amongst ourselves.

299
00:37:48,860 --> 00:37:51,560
We have so many enemies now.

300
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:09,320
Jon.

301
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:12,210
A raven came from the Citadel.

302
00:38:13,550 --> 00:38:15,030
A white raven.

303
00:38:18,320 --> 00:38:19,710
Winter is here.

304
00:38:32,070 --> 00:38:34,680
Well, Father always promised, didn't he?

305
00:38:49,460 --> 00:38:52,260
The last time a Tyrell came to Dorne,

306
00:38:52,260 --> 00:38:54,100
he was assassinated.

307
00:38:54,630 --> 00:38:57,130
100 red scorpions, was it?

308
00:38:57,380 --> 00:38:59,760
You have nothing to fear from us, Lady Olenna.

309
00:39:00,040 --> 00:39:02,040
You murder your own prince,

310
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:03,990
but you expect me to trust you?

311
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:07,080
We invited you to Dorne because we needed your help.

312
00:39:07,120 --> 00:39:09,570
You came to Dorne because you needed our help.

313
00:39:10,140 --> 00:39:11,830
What is your name again?

314
00:39:12,740 --> 00:39:14,120
Barbaro?

315
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,060
Obara.

316
00:39:15,070 --> 00:39:18,260
Obara. You look like an angry little boy.

317
00:39:18,260 --> 00:39:20,800
Don't presume to tell me what I need.

318
00:39:21,290 --> 00:39:24,080
Forgive my sister. What she lacks in diplomacy, she makes--

319
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:27,340
Do shut up, dear. Anything from you?

320
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:29,520
No? Good.

321
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:31,710
Let the grown women speak.

322
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:36,490
The Lannisters have declared war on House Tyrell.

323
00:39:37,030 --> 00:39:38,950
They have declared war on Dorne.

324
00:39:39,780 --> 00:39:43,340
We must be allies now if we wish to survive.

325
00:39:44,660 --> 00:39:46,710
Cersei stole the future from me.

326
00:39:47,460 --> 00:39:48,970
She killed my son.

327
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:51,130
She killed my grandson.

328
00:39:51,950 --> 00:39:53,690
She killed my granddaughter.

329
00:39:55,030 --> 00:39:57,500
Survival is not what I'm after now.

330
00:39:58,060 --> 00:39:59,680
You're absolutely right.

331
00:40:00,290 --> 00:40:02,150
I chose the wrong words.

332
00:40:02,810 --> 00:40:05,140
It is not survival I offer.

333
00:40:05,500 --> 00:40:07,550
It is your heart's desire.

334
00:40:09,730 --> 00:40:12,690
And what is my heart's desire?

335
00:40:14,230 --> 00:40:15,480
Vengeance.

336
00:40:16,440 --> 00:40:17,770
Justice.

337
00:40:21,570 --> 00:40:23,030
Fire and blood.

338
00:40:30,130 --> 00:40:31,710
Your ships are nearly ready.

339
00:40:32,930 --> 00:40:34,710
I saw them painting the sails.

340
00:40:38,540 --> 00:40:41,600
I'm curious to see how the Dothraki do on the poison water.

341
00:40:42,350 --> 00:40:43,900
You're not coming with us.

342
00:40:46,650 --> 00:40:48,070
New strategy?

343
00:40:49,830 --> 00:40:52,440
You want the Second Sons to attack from the west coast?

344
00:40:53,530 --> 00:40:55,570
If we take Casterly Rock,

345
00:40:56,360 --> 00:40:58,240
the Lannisters will have nowhere to run

346
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,690
when you hit King's Landing.

347
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:01,690
You're not going to Westeros.

348
00:41:02,060 --> 00:41:04,240
You're staying here with the Second Sons.

349
00:41:05,130 --> 00:41:07,370
There's finally peace in Meereen.

350
00:41:07,810 --> 00:41:11,000
You will keep the peace while the people choose their own leaders.

351
00:41:12,010 --> 00:41:13,360
Fuck Meereen.

352
00:41:13,980 --> 00:41:15,350
Fuck the people.

353
00:41:16,090 --> 00:41:18,220
I'm here for you, not them.

354
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,670
You promised me.

355
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:22,960
"My sword is yours. My life is yours."

356
00:41:23,930 --> 00:41:25,570
This is what I command.

357
00:41:27,500 --> 00:41:29,260
If I'm going to rule in Westeros,

358
00:41:29,260 --> 00:41:30,930
I'll need to make alliances.

359
00:41:32,190 --> 00:41:35,780
The best way to make alliances is with marriage.

360
00:41:38,980 --> 00:41:40,820
Who are you marrying this time?

361
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:44,200
I don't know. Maybe no one.

362
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:46,940
But you need to lure all the noble houses to the table?

363
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:49,480
Are you a queen or fish bait?

364
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:54,970
I can't bring a lover to Westeros.

365
00:41:54,970 --> 00:41:57,230
A king wouldn't think twice about it.

366
00:41:57,230 --> 00:42:00,070
So that's what you want? To be my mistress?

367
00:42:00,070 --> 00:42:03,460
I'm not proud. I don't care what perfumed aristocrat

368
00:42:03,460 --> 00:42:05,630
sits beside you in the throne room.

369
00:42:05,760 --> 00:42:09,120
I don't want a crown. I want you.

370
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:17,550
I love you.

371
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:19,550
And I make you happy.

372
00:42:21,300 --> 00:42:22,480
You know I do.

373
00:42:24,660 --> 00:42:28,530
Bring me with you. Let me fight for you.

374
00:42:36,290 --> 00:42:37,490
I can't.

375
00:42:47,370 --> 00:42:48,810
The dwarf told you to do this?

376
00:42:48,810 --> 00:42:50,750
No one tells me to do anything.

377
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:53,480
Clever fellow. Can't argue with his logic.

378
00:42:54,120 --> 00:42:55,660
I'm no use to you over there.

379
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:56,860
Don't get angry.

380
00:42:56,860 --> 00:43:00,250
I'm not angry. I'm full of self-pity.

381
00:43:00,540 --> 00:43:01,930
Who comes after you?

382
00:43:01,930 --> 00:43:05,320
Who can ever follow Daenerys Stormborn, the Mother of Dragons?

383
00:43:05,330 --> 00:43:07,630
A great number of women, I imagine.

384
00:43:14,040 --> 00:43:15,740
Specific orders will be left for you

385
00:43:15,740 --> 00:43:18,890
regarding the welfare of Meereen and the Bay of Dragons.

386
00:43:19,210 --> 00:43:20,710
Bay of Dragons?

387
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:23,300
We can't call it Slaver's Bay anymore, can we?

388
00:43:26,910 --> 00:43:29,940
You'll get that throne you want so badly, I'm sure of it.

389
00:43:31,490 --> 00:43:33,130
I hope it brings you happiness.

390
00:43:38,780 --> 00:43:40,860
I pity the lords of Westeros.

391
00:43:41,740 --> 00:43:43,790
They have no idea what's coming for them.

392
00:43:44,720 --> 00:43:47,350
Farewell, Daario Naharis.

393
00:44:06,840 --> 00:44:07,950
How did he take it?

394
00:44:08,810 --> 00:44:09,840
No tears.

395
00:44:12,900 --> 00:44:14,190
I know it was hard for you.

396
00:44:15,730 --> 00:44:17,620
You turned away a man who truly loves you

397
00:44:17,630 --> 00:44:20,410
because he would have been a liability in the Seven Kingdoms.

398
00:44:23,390 --> 00:44:26,850
That's the kind of self-sacrifice that makes for a good ruler,

399
00:44:27,150 --> 00:44:28,750
if it's any consolation.

400
00:44:32,140 --> 00:44:33,100
It's not.

401
00:44:33,900 --> 00:44:36,240
No, I suppose not.

402
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:37,730
I'm terrible at consoling.

403
00:44:37,730 --> 00:44:39,610
Yes, you really are.

404
00:44:43,570 --> 00:44:47,580
All right, how about the fact that this is actually happening?

405
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:51,950
You have your armies, you have your ships,

406
00:44:51,950 --> 00:44:53,430
you have your dragons.

407
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:56,200
Everything you've ever wanted

408
00:44:56,220 --> 00:44:58,810
since you were old enough to want anything,

409
00:44:59,190 --> 00:45:00,770
it's all yours for the taking.

410
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:04,310
Are you afraid?

411
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:08,790
Good.

412
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:11,960
You're in the great game now.

413
00:45:12,890 --> 00:45:14,920
And the great game's terrifying.

414
00:45:15,750 --> 00:45:17,820
The only people who aren't afraid of failure

415
00:45:17,820 --> 00:45:19,600
are madmen like your father.

416
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:24,020
Do you know what frightens me?

417
00:45:25,900 --> 00:45:28,620
I said farewell to a man who loves me.

418
00:45:30,460 --> 00:45:32,260
A man I thought I cared for.

419
00:45:34,360 --> 00:45:35,740
And I felt nothing.

420
00:45:37,670 --> 00:45:39,500
Just impatient to get on with it.

421
00:45:42,810 --> 00:45:44,570
He wasn't the first to love you

422
00:45:45,860 --> 00:45:47,540
and he won't be the last.

423
00:45:51,920 --> 00:45:56,900
Well, you have completely failed to console me.

424
00:45:59,300 --> 00:46:03,320
For what it's worth, I've been a cynic for as long as I can remember.

425
00:46:04,030 --> 00:46:06,780
Everyone's always asking me to believe in things--

426
00:46:06,870 --> 00:46:10,270
family, gods, kings, myself.

427
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,560
It was often tempting

428
00:46:12,570 --> 00:46:15,050
until I saw where belief got people.

429
00:46:16,470 --> 00:46:19,190
So I said no, thank you to belief.

430
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:22,320
And yet here I am.

431
00:46:25,040 --> 00:46:26,890
I believe in you.

432
00:46:30,030 --> 00:46:31,690
It's embarrassing, really.

433
00:46:33,900 --> 00:46:35,370
I'd swear you my sword,

434
00:46:35,370 --> 00:46:38,560
but I don't actually own a sword.

435
00:46:38,900 --> 00:46:40,870
It's your counsel I need.

436
00:46:41,720 --> 00:46:42,950
It's yours.

437
00:46:43,410 --> 00:46:44,870
Now and always.

438
00:46:46,270 --> 00:46:47,080
Good.

439
00:46:49,350 --> 00:46:50,770
I, um...

440
00:46:51,610 --> 00:46:53,200
I had something made for you.

441
00:46:55,050 --> 00:46:57,480
I'm not sure if it's right.

442
00:47:06,860 --> 00:47:08,120
Tyrion Lannister,

443
00:47:09,730 --> 00:47:11,330
I name you Hand of the Queen.

444
00:47:46,110 --> 00:47:48,400
You're not one of mine, are you?

445
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:49,810
No, my lord.

446
00:47:49,860 --> 00:47:51,280
Didn't think so.

447
00:47:52,620 --> 00:47:53,970
Too pretty.

448
00:47:58,600 --> 00:48:01,180
Where are my damn moron sons?

449
00:48:01,400 --> 00:48:04,900
Black Walder and Lothar promised to be here by midday.

450
00:48:05,550 --> 00:48:06,910
They're here, my lord.

451
00:48:07,390 --> 00:48:10,520
Well, what are they doing, trimming their cunt hairs?

452
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:12,430
Tell them to come here now.

453
00:48:13,020 --> 00:48:14,890
But they're already here, my lord.

454
00:48:19,170 --> 00:48:22,160
Here, my lord.

455
00:48:40,560 --> 00:48:42,450
They weren't easy to carve.

456
00:48:44,280 --> 00:48:46,100
Especially Black Walder.

457
00:48:47,630 --> 00:48:48,650
What...

458
00:48:55,620 --> 00:48:57,290
My name is Arya Stark.

459
00:48:57,780 --> 00:48:59,180
I want you to know that.

460
00:48:59,880 --> 00:49:02,070
The last thing you're ever going to see

461
00:49:02,150 --> 00:49:05,150
is a Stark smiling down at you as you die.

462
00:49:59,810 --> 00:50:01,190
Forgive me, my lady...

463
00:50:03,150 --> 00:50:04,490
if you're at prayer.

464
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:07,930
I'm done with all that.

465
00:50:10,570 --> 00:50:12,860
I came here every day when I was a girl.

466
00:50:14,550 --> 00:50:16,300
I prayed to be somewhere else.

467
00:50:17,820 --> 00:50:19,760
Back then I only thought about what I wanted,

468
00:50:19,760 --> 00:50:21,160
never about what I had.

469
00:50:24,980 --> 00:50:26,550
I was a stupid girl.

470
00:50:26,950 --> 00:50:28,280
You were a child.

471
00:50:32,240 --> 00:50:33,460
What do you want?

472
00:50:34,910 --> 00:50:36,700
I thought you knew what I wanted.

473
00:50:37,290 --> 00:50:38,330
I was wrong.

474
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:41,490
No, you weren't.

475
00:50:44,380 --> 00:50:45,780
Every time I'm faced with a decision,

476
00:50:45,780 --> 00:50:48,340
I close my eyes and see the same picture.

477
00:50:49,780 --> 00:50:52,230
Whenever I consider an action, I ask myself

478
00:50:53,480 --> 00:50:57,360
will this action help to make this picture a reality?

479
00:50:59,620 --> 00:51:01,230
Pull it out of my mind

480
00:51:02,340 --> 00:51:03,720
and into the world?

481
00:51:06,540 --> 00:51:08,870
And I only act if the answer is yes.

482
00:51:12,120 --> 00:51:16,740
A picture of me on the Iron Throne...

483
00:51:19,520 --> 00:51:21,160
and you by my side.

484
00:51:31,410 --> 00:51:32,770
It's a pretty picture.

485
00:51:39,350 --> 00:51:42,280
News of this battle will spread quickly through the Seven Kingdoms.

486
00:51:42,630 --> 00:51:44,970
I've declared for House Stark for all to hear.

487
00:51:46,240 --> 00:51:48,530
You've declared for other houses before, Lord Baelish.

488
00:51:48,530 --> 00:51:51,050
It's never stopped you from serving yourself.

489
00:51:51,550 --> 00:51:53,320
The past is gone for good.

490
00:51:54,140 --> 00:51:55,740
You can sit here mourning its departure

491
00:51:55,740 --> 00:51:58,780
or you can prepare for the future.

492
00:51:58,780 --> 00:52:00,720
You, my love,

493
00:52:01,600 --> 00:52:03,360
are the future of House Stark.

494
00:52:05,390 --> 00:52:07,260
Who should the North rally behind?

495
00:52:08,590 --> 00:52:10,690
A trueborn daughter of Ned and Catelyn Stark

496
00:52:10,690 --> 00:52:12,230
born here at Winterfell

497
00:52:13,070 --> 00:52:15,710
or a motherless bastard born in the south?

498
00:52:42,530 --> 00:52:44,060
This is where I leave you.

499
00:52:44,930 --> 00:52:46,300
You're not coming with us?

500
00:52:48,250 --> 00:52:50,270
The Wall is not just ice and stone.

501
00:52:51,790 --> 00:52:54,860
Ancient spells were carved into its foundations.

502
00:52:56,440 --> 00:53:01,120
Strong magic to protect men from what lies beyond.

503
00:53:02,130 --> 00:53:05,160
And while it stands, the dead cannot pass.

504
00:53:05,770 --> 00:53:07,260
I cannot pass.

505
00:53:23,820 --> 00:53:24,880
Where will you go?

506
00:53:25,830 --> 00:53:27,280
The great war is coming

507
00:53:27,690 --> 00:53:29,450
and I still fight for the living.

508
00:53:32,410 --> 00:53:33,540
I'll do what I can...

509
00:53:35,670 --> 00:53:36,820
as long as I can.

510
00:53:41,950 --> 00:53:43,340
Thank you, Uncle Benjen.

511
00:53:44,040 --> 00:53:46,000
I wish you both good fortune.

512
00:54:25,720 --> 00:54:28,040
Are you sure you're ready for this?

513
00:54:28,260 --> 00:54:30,120
I'm the Three-Eyed Raven now.

514
00:54:31,590 --> 00:54:33,470
I have to be ready for this.

515
00:55:07,900 --> 00:55:08,770
Ned?

516
00:55:09,830 --> 00:55:10,810
Lyanna.

517
00:55:12,860 --> 00:55:13,930
Is that you?

518
00:55:18,440 --> 00:55:19,960
Is that really you?

519
00:55:25,320 --> 00:55:26,700
You're not a dream?

520
00:55:28,550 --> 00:55:29,950
No, I'm not a dream.

521
00:55:32,390 --> 00:55:33,370
I'm here.

522
00:55:35,840 --> 00:55:36,860
Right here.

523
00:55:37,550 --> 00:55:39,510
I've missed you, big brother.

524
00:55:43,580 --> 00:55:44,870
I've missed you, too.

525
00:55:49,790 --> 00:55:51,420
I want to be brave.

526
00:55:55,380 --> 00:55:56,230
You are.

527
00:55:56,510 --> 00:55:57,600
I'm not.

528
00:56:01,610 --> 00:56:03,140
I don't want to die.

529
00:56:04,870 --> 00:56:06,430
You're not going to die.

530
00:56:11,150 --> 00:56:12,420
Get her some water.

531
00:56:12,460 --> 00:56:14,780
- No, no water. - Is there a maester?

532
00:56:14,780 --> 00:56:16,530
Listen to me, Ned.

533
00:56:23,750 --> 00:56:26,230
If Robert finds out, he'll--

534
00:56:26,230 --> 00:56:27,300
you know he will.

535
00:56:28,480 --> 00:56:30,160
You have to protect him.

536
00:56:33,500 --> 00:56:34,960
Promise me, Ned.

537
00:56:37,970 --> 00:56:39,260
Promise me.

538
00:56:51,750 --> 00:56:53,220
Promise me, Ned.

539
00:56:58,940 --> 00:57:00,030
Promise me.

540
00:57:30,750 --> 00:57:33,400
You can't expect Knights of the Vale

541
00:57:33,400 --> 00:57:36,140
to side with wildling invaders.

542
00:57:36,140 --> 00:57:40,080
We didn't invade. We were invited.

543
00:57:40,080 --> 00:57:41,450
Not by me.

544
00:57:42,090 --> 00:57:43,870
The free folk, the northerners,

545
00:57:43,870 --> 00:57:45,970
and the Knights of the Vale fought bravely,

546
00:57:45,970 --> 00:57:47,700
fought together, and we won.

547
00:57:49,080 --> 00:57:50,490
My father used to say

548
00:57:50,490 --> 00:57:53,500
we find our true friends on the battlefield.

549
00:57:53,810 --> 00:57:55,950
The Boltons are defeated.

550
00:57:56,330 --> 00:57:57,870
The war is over.

551
00:57:58,200 --> 00:57:59,880
Winter has come.

552
00:58:00,070 --> 00:58:01,170
If the maesters are right,

553
00:58:01,170 --> 00:58:03,580
it'll be the coldest one in a thousand years.

554
00:58:04,140 --> 00:58:07,340
We should ride home and wait out the coming storms.

555
00:58:07,340 --> 00:58:09,050
The war is not over.

556
00:58:09,770 --> 00:58:11,480
And I promise you, friend,

557
00:58:11,900 --> 00:58:14,530
the true enemy won't wait out the storm.

558
00:58:15,120 --> 00:58:16,680
He brings the storm.

559
00:58:36,610 --> 00:58:40,140
Your son was butchered at the Red Wedding, Lord Manderly,

560
00:58:40,640 --> 00:58:42,290
but you refused the call.

561
00:58:45,880 --> 00:58:48,620
You swore allegiance to House Stark, Lord Glover,

562
00:58:48,900 --> 00:58:51,380
but in their hour of greatest need,

563
00:58:51,830 --> 00:58:53,540
you refused the call.

564
00:58:55,700 --> 00:58:58,180
And you, Lord Cerwyn,

565
00:58:58,600 --> 00:59:01,600
your father was skinned alive by Ramsay Bolton.

566
00:59:01,810 --> 00:59:04,310
Still you refused the call.

567
00:59:07,410 --> 00:59:09,660
But House Mormont remembers.

568
00:59:11,430 --> 00:59:13,870
The North remembers.

569
00:59:14,290 --> 00:59:16,850
We know no king but the King in the North

570
00:59:16,850 --> 00:59:18,560
whose name is Stark.

571
00:59:20,680 --> 00:59:22,290
I don't care if he's a bastard.

572
00:59:22,300 --> 00:59:24,720
Ned Stark's blood runs through his veins.

573
00:59:24,810 --> 00:59:29,170
He's my king from this day until his last day.

574
00:59:46,160 --> 00:59:47,950
Lady Mormont speaks harshly

575
00:59:48,790 --> 00:59:50,080
and truly.

576
00:59:54,590 --> 00:59:57,650
My son died for Robb Stark, the Young Wolf.

577
00:59:58,720 --> 01:00:01,670
I didn't think we'd find another king in my lifetime.

578
01:00:02,090 --> 01:00:04,240
I didn't commit my men to your cause

579
01:00:04,590 --> 01:00:07,050
'cause I didn't want more Manderlys dying for nothing.

580
01:00:09,600 --> 01:00:10,700
But I was wrong.

581
01:00:16,930 --> 01:00:18,990
Jon Snow avenged the Red Wedding.

582
01:00:19,600 --> 01:00:21,490
He is the White Wolf.

583
01:00:21,980 --> 01:00:23,930
The King in the North.

584
01:00:32,130 --> 01:00:34,900
I did not fight beside you on the field

585
01:00:34,900 --> 01:00:38,110
and I will regret that until my dying day.

586
01:00:38,830 --> 01:00:42,240
A man can only admit when he was wrong

587
01:00:42,620 --> 01:00:44,250
and ask forgiveness.

588
01:00:47,390 --> 01:00:49,340
There's nothing to forgive, my lord.

589
01:00:52,270 --> 01:00:54,240
There will be more fights to come.

590
01:00:54,930 --> 01:00:58,190
House Glover will stand behind House Stark

591
01:00:58,580 --> 01:01:00,930
as we have for a thousand years.

592
01:01:02,410 --> 01:01:04,780
And I will stand behind Jon Snow...

593
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:08,870
the King in the North!

594
01:01:11,180 --> 01:01:12,740
The King in the North!

595
01:01:14,180 --> 01:01:17,820
The King in the North! The King in the North!

596
01:01:17,830 --> 01:01:21,000
The King in the North! The King in the North!

597
01:01:21,000 --> 01:01:24,330
The King in the North! The King in the North!

598
01:01:24,460 --> 01:01:27,860
The King in the North! The King in the North!

599
01:01:28,200 --> 01:01:31,490
The King in the North! The King in the North!

600
01:01:31,780 --> 01:01:35,200
The King in the North! The King in the North!

601
01:01:35,360 --> 01:01:38,790
The King in the North! The King in the North!

602
01:01:38,790 --> 01:01:42,170
The King in the North! The King in the North!

603
01:01:42,170 --> 01:01:45,330
The King in the North! The King in the North!

604
01:01:45,350 --> 01:01:48,580
The King in the North! The King in the North!

605
01:01:48,630 --> 01:01:51,690
The King in the North! The King in the North!

606
01:01:57,740 --> 01:01:59,450
Company halt!

607
01:02:02,610 --> 01:02:03,530
Halt!

608
01:02:05,850 --> 01:02:07,880
Halt!

609
01:02:20,100 --> 01:02:20,970
Come on.

610
01:03:15,460 --> 01:03:18,440
I now proclaim Cersei of the House Lannister

611
01:03:19,570 --> 01:03:21,280
First of Her Name,

612
01:03:22,110 --> 01:03:25,060
Queen of the Andals and the First Men,

613
01:03:25,840 --> 01:03:28,890
Protector of the Seven Kingdoms.

614
01:04:15,020 --> 01:04:16,950
Long may she reign.

615
01:04:16,950 --> 01:04:19,050
Long may she reign.

